  1946	/**Function*************************************************************
  1947	
  1948	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if an stmap area-sensitive mode should reject a cut.]
  1949	
  1950	  Description [The area-sensitive guards are evaluated after matching the
  1951	  candidate cut because their hypotheses need the candidate's actual mapper
  1952	  area. In stmap6 exact-area recovery, a wide high-fanout cut is rejected only
  1953	  when the existing match has slack and the candidate does not save at least
  1954	  half an inverter area. In stmap7, the area-saving override additionally
  1955	  requires more than two inverter delays of slack and excludes the highest
  1956	  fanout-risk bucket. In stmap8, the override is further rejected when the
  1957	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
  1958	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
  1959	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
  1960	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
  1961	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
  1962	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
  1963	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. In
