The patch builds, but the new stmap53 exception can activate under the wrong first-pass conditions because it checks pressure-vector capacity instead of the measured pressure population/severe branch.

Review comment:

- [P2] Gate the exception on pressure entries — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:1537-1537
  For designs with `Feedback >= 0.80` but fewer than 8000 sink-pressure entries, this still enables the new pressure-near exception whenever the allocated pressure vector happens to have capacity >= 8000. `s_nStmap45SclPressureRatios` is the vector length/capacity passed for AIG-ID lookup, not the sink-pressure population used by `stmap53` to identify severe-pressure runs, so the exception can admit cuts based on max AIG ID rather than the intended pressure threshold.
